            <ArticleTitle>Retrieval of dislodged coronary intravascular ultrasound catheter with embolic protection device.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A retained fractured segment of an intravascular ultrasound catheter in the coronary artery during percutaneous coronary intervention is a rare occurrence. We describe our experience with successful retrieval of a fractured IVUS catheter fragment in a previously stented left anterior descending artery using a distal embolic protection device.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
